# 15. Dependency and Source-of-Truth Review

Identify only proven dependencies:

- Frontend components
- Shared UI components
- API clients
- Routes
- Services
- Database tables
- Migrations
- Redis/cache
- Authentication
- RBAC
- Capabilities
- ACL
- Runtime mode
- Kill Switch
- Scheduler
- Worker
- Provider integrations
- Settings
- Nginx
- PM2
- Deployment scripts

Before creating a field, route, service or setting, identify the existing
owner.

Never duplicate:

- Settings
- Tokens
- API keys
- Credentials
- Integrations
- Connection metadata
- Capability Matrix
- Agent registry
- Permission rules
- Runtime mode
- Kill Switch
- Scheduler state
- Worker state
- Provider configuration
- Cache
- Database state
- API contracts
- Audit/history
- Notification configuration

If an owner exists:

- Reuse it
- Extend it
- Connect to it
- Or migrate the old path into it

Never create a parallel implementation.

